add(P_("Surya is the stronger reader of Latin text and the weaker reader of Devanagari. It reads " + SUR.card.epic + " of 300 EPIC numbers, including all " + B3.classes[0][1] + " that the pipeline misread in the prefix, because it reads the whole line and does not share the pipeline's crop. On names it is behind (" + SUR.card.name + " against " + B3.fields.name + "; " + SUR.card.relName + " against " + B3.fields.relName + "), with the single-glyph errors consensus exists for (पुर्णिमा for पूर्णिमा, माधुर for माथुर) and a dropped nukta in विलेज़ on most of Dadri's village cards. Card for card the pipeline is ahead (" + B3.fully + " to " + SUR.cards6 + "), in Dadri and Jewar; Surya is ahead in Noida, where the pipeline's two faults are. The engines are complementary rather than ranked, and the cost differs by an order of magnitude: " + Math.round(SUR.seconds / 10) + " seconds a page on a GPU against four or five on a CPU."));
add(P_("Of " + B3.disagreements + " cells on which the model's transcription and the pipeline disagreed, adjudication found the pipeline right once and the transcription " + (B3.disagreements - B3.annotatorWrong - B3.ambiguous) + " times, with two glyphs ambiguous at 300 dpi. That record is the transcriber grading itself and is not independence; Surya, a third reader that shares nothing with either, agrees with the transcription on " + SUR.card.epic + " EPIC numbers and every age, which is some protection against a systematic transcription error in the fields that matter most, but a human reading of the ten pages remains the outstanding check."));
