add(figure("fig5_translit_ablation.png", "Figure 5. Transliteration accuracy by configuration on the full 113-name set; Table 3 gives the split by whether the name occurs in the seed corpus.", 4.2));
add(P_("The rule-only errors are conventions rather than phonetic mistakes: सिंह → Sinh for Singh, धीर → Dheer for Dhir, फिरोज → Firoj for Firoz. The re-ranker learns most of these from context, and that gain, 87% to 92% overall and 62% to 81% on the unseen names, is the generalisation result. The perfect score of the full engine is not one: the lexicon is an exact-match table built from a corpus that contains 92 of the 113 names, and the override table that closes the gap was edited after the evaluation set was drawn. The residual errors on unseen names (Dheer, Ijaj, Firoj, Mangate) are the j/z and ee/i conventions of north Indian Roman spelling, which a larger seed corpus would settle."));
