add(H1("Appendix A. Roll page and cover layout"));
add(figure("fig1b_cover_redacted.png", "Figure A1. Cover page of a part PDF (pixelated). The top block identifies state, constituency and part; the middle block lists the administrative units; the bottom block gives polling-station details, the elector count and the last serial number.", 3.4));
add(H1("Appendix B. Annotation guidelines for the benchmark"));
add(P_("Render the page at 300 dpi. Transcribe every field exactly as printed, including leading zeros, punctuation in house numbers and the roll's own spelling of a name even if it is inconsistent with the same name elsewhere. Serial is the grid position. Record the relation type as printed (पिता/माता/पति) and gender as printed. Do not consult the OCR output while annotating. The development page was transcribed by one annotator by eye."));
add(P_("Test set (Section 6.3). Ten pages were drawn with a fixed random seed (one page per sampled part, between its third and third-from-last), rendered at 300 dpi and cut into two halves. A vision-language model (Claude Fable 5.1) transcribed each half under the rules above; the pipeline was scored against it, and every disagreeing cell was re-examined on a crop of the card at three times the size. The transcription was corrected only where the crop showed the pipeline to be right (one cell); two cells that stayed ambiguous are scored against the pipeline. The transcriptions are personal data and are not released; they are available to reviewers."));
add(P_("Synthetic page. paper/analysis/make_synthetic_page.py draws a page in the roll's geometry (three columns, ten rows, serial box, EPIC at the top right, photograph box, the four labelled lines) with names assembled at random from common given names and surnames, EPIC numbers in an unissued series and random ages, and writes it with its truth file to test/fixtures. The final build reads " + SYN.fully + " of its 30 cards fully correct, every name, relation, age and gender, " + SYN.epic + " of 30 EPIC numbers and " + SYN.house + " of 30 house numbers; its errors (" + SYN.note + ") are the two systematic faults of Section 6.3, which is what makes it useful as a regression test."));
