add(bullet("Statistics and cross-constituency analysis: node paper/analysis/gbn_stats_build.cjs (reads the dashboard, writes paper/data/gbn_stats.json); EPIC prefix repair scope: node paper/analysis/epic_series_repair.cjs"));
add(bullet("Booth-level aggregates and figures: paper/data/gbn_stats.json; python3 paper/make_figs.py; node paper/build_paper.cjs"));
add(H1("Appendix H. Engineering notes"));

add(P_("Page geometry is not fixed. Uttarakhand's rolls declare a 1983 × 2806 pt page: at a fixed 300 dpi that is eleven times the pixels of an A4 roll with no more detail, and the first run on them was four times slower and missed cards. The renderer now scales the DPI so that any page gets the pixel size an A4 page gets (renderDpi in src/pdf.ts). The lesson is procedural: pdfinfo on one file of a new state before the first run."));
add(P_("Collecting from the CDN. The CDN answers a burst of requests, and every request from the rented server's address, with HTTP 406, so PDFs are downloaded on a desktop machine at a throttled rate and copied to the server; only 404 means a file is absent. Constituency numbers are taken from the portal's district-to-constituency endpoint and never typed by hand, after a number guessed from memory put one constituency's rows on the dashboard under another's name."));
add(P_("The DELETED-stamp detector in numbers. Grey ink is a pixel value from 100 to 234 of 255 after the card is rescaled to 200 dpi; text edges are removed by discarding grey within two pixels of black. On the 35 calibration cards the first measure (densest sheared band, all grey ink) was at least 0.168 on every stamped card and at most 0.172 on clean cards, so the two overlap on text-heavy cards and the threshold of 0.15 alone would over-detect; the second measure (grey ink away from text) was at least 0.045 on stamped and at most 0.035 on clean cards with no overlap, and its threshold of 0.04 is what decides. Both measures are written to the row so that the thresholds can be revisited without rescanning."));
add(P_("Tests and switches. Thirteen test files cover consensus, cover parsing, CSV output, voting, layout, merge, the name memory, normalisation, official part lists, oversized pages, the stamp features and transliteration. Environment switches turn stages off for ablation without a code change (OCR_EPIC_VOTE, OCR_CONSENSUS, OCR_NAME_LEXICON, OCR_NAME_MEMORY); the evaluation cache must be cleared between ablation runs."));

